    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d94c348c_6431723d",
        "filename": "android/pandora/server/proto/pandora/host.proto",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 210,
      "author": {
        "id": 1881539
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-06T10:16:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I know that this is a protobuf recommendation to always define an `UNSPECIFIED` so that servers will be able to handle a newer value set by the client and not take it as the 0 value.\n\nHowever here I don\u0027t think it makes sense to have an `UNSPECIFIED` value as I don\u0027t see what a client can give as meaning to it.\nAlso we are less subject to have clients and server out of sync as the version of the two should be in our control.\nAnd furthermore it\u0027s very unlikely that we would need to change this enum one day (And if we do I think we will have a lot more changes to make :) ).",
      "revId": "26f2aaf62a46d8041e210a9848ad8e8302cb3a16",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6322e8c7_585beb53",
        "filename": "android/pandora/server/proto/pandora/host.proto",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 210,
      "author": {
        "id": 1958203
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-06T16:31:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The reason I want UNSPECIFIED is so that, if the caller fails to pass it in, we can distinguish it from BREDR (or whatever we assign to value 0). We could also do that by testing for whether the field is set, but if (and when) we forget to do that I don\u0027t want to silently get wrong data.\n\nWe can\u0027t just skip the 0 value since it is required to be defined (as per https://developers.google.com/protocol-buffers/docs/proto3#default)",
      "parentUuid": "d94c348c_6431723d",
      "revId": "26f2aaf62a46d8041e210a9848ad8e8302cb3a16",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0ee42d2d_7c652e5e",
        "filename": "android/pandora/server/proto/pandora/host.proto",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 210,
      "author": {
        "id": 1904823
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-07T02:23:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If we allow `TRANSPORT_UNSPECIFIED`, we are basically saying that the `Tranport` field is optional. If this is intended I\u0027m fine with this modification (but we should indicate it in its description), if it\u0027s not I agree with David.",
      "parentUuid": "6322e8c7_585beb53",
      "revId": "26f2aaf62a46d8041e210a9848ad8e8302cb3a16",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f2fd37a6_1b6dc79f",
        "filename": "android/pandora/server/proto/pandora/host.proto",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 210,
      "author": {
        "id": 1881539
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-07T07:58:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e if the caller fails to pass it in, we can distinguish it from BREDR\n\nAh I didn\u0027t took into account that it will take the default value if it\u0027s not set.\nWe maybe could use `required` here. But as the thing that will pas this value is the server, I think that defaulting to BREDR (by using it as the 0 value) if not specified is not a bad behavior here.",
      "parentUuid": "0ee42d2d_7c652e5e",
      "revId": "26f2aaf62a46d8041e210a9848ad8e8302cb3a16",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "131a5f2d_8077ab4a",
        "filename": "android/pandora/server/src/com/android/pandora/Security.kt",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 134,
      "author": {
        "id": 1881539
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-06T10:16:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think we should `error` here instead of doing it afterwards",
      "revId": "26f2aaf62a46d8041e210a9848ad8e8302cb3a16",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "33df226e_32bd2082",
        "filename": "android/pandora/server/src/com/android/pandora/Security.kt",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 134,
      "author": {
        "id": 1958203
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-06T16:31:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t want to error here, since it is still possible in most cases to figure out the right pairing variant. So we just leave the transport unset, as most of the time the user only cares about the variant.\n\nErroring here means we break OnPair() for TYPE_DUAL devices entirely, rather than only breaking it for dual mode devices when using an ambiguous pairing variant.",
      "parentUuid": "131a5f2d_8077ab4a",
      "revId": "26f2aaf62a46d8041e210a9848ad8e8302cb3a16",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "58fc03e6_72814aaf",
        "filename": "android/pandora/server/src/com/android/pandora/Security.kt",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 134,
      "author": {
        "id": 1904823
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-07T02:23:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is there any case where this happens? If we don\u0027t know any, I would indeed raise an error so at least we can catch it the first time it happens to understand why.",
      "parentUuid": "33df226e_32bd2082",
      "revId": "26f2aaf62a46d8041e210a9848ad8e8302cb3a16",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "939532e2_36100bf3",
        "filename": "android/pandora/server/src/com/android/pandora/Security.kt",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 134,
      "author": {
        "id": 1958203
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-07T18:04:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This will happen if we pair with a dual-mode device, since then we can\u0027t tell what transport we are using for the pairing.",
      "parentUuid": "58fc03e6_72814aaf",
      "revId": "26f2aaf62a46d8041e210a9848ad8e8302cb3a16",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
